飾り付けた

21
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:26,000
Black paper, brown, brown

22
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:29,800
信じてくれたなら

23
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:34,100
When you lost him or young

24
00:02:34,100 --> 00:02:37,600
Forever with your soul

25
00:02:37,600 --> 00:02:41,600
見上げれば輝く

26
00:02:41,600 --> 00:02:43,900
月のように

27
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:52,200
トーリー

28
00:02:52,200 --> 00:02:53,900
キッド

29
00:02:53,900 --> 00:02:55,900
キッド

30
00:02:55,900 --> 00:02:56,900
キッド

31
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:57,900
キッド

32
00:02:57,900 --> 00:02:58,700
キッド

33
00:02:58,700 --> 00:02:59,900
キッド

34
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,600
It's not like it was my decision.

35
00:03:02,340 --> 00:03:04,700
And I would really rather not talk about it, okay?

36
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:06,100
Yeah, fine.

37
00:03:06,180 --> 00:03:08,660
But do you think you could at least give us an idea of where we're going?

38
00:03:09,020 --> 00:03:10,720
Yeah, that's fair enough.

39
00:03:12,020 --> 00:03:14,500
We're going to a place called Sarcophagus.

40
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:15,640
Sarcophagus?

41
00:03:15,960 --> 00:03:16,660
That's right.

42
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:18,700
And it's aptly named, too.

43
00:03:19,400 --> 00:03:20,340
And why's that?

44
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:24,540
It used to be just an ordinary old village like any other.

45
00:03:24,540 --> 00:03:26,640
But that was 20 years ago.

46
00:03:27,260 --> 00:03:28,320
Things have changed.

47
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:30,700
Changed how?

48
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:35,680
Well, one day, its citizens suddenly disappeared.

49
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:38,720
Every last one of them.

50
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:39,620
What?

51
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:42,480
How could all those people vanish in the thin air?

52
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:44,800
To this day, no one knows.

53
00:03:45,360 --> 00:03:50,240
The people sent to investigate vanished just like the village's citizens, gone without a trace.

54
00:03:51,240 --> 00:03:54,580
After a while, the investigation was given up.

55
00:03:54,660 --> 00:03:56,480
It would have been too dangerous to continue.

56
00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:00,340
The entire area was locked down to prevent further disappearances.

57
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:02,680
That's where we're going.

58
00:04:02,680 --> 00:04:09,460
There it is.

59
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:11,920
That Sarcophagus.

60
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,700
The last magic tool.

61
00:04:19,100 --> 00:04:20,980
Mission Impossible for Unarmed Kid?

62
00:04:20,980 --> 00:04:24,340
See that?

63
00:04:24,340 --> 00:04:27,800
That wall was hastily built.

64
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:32,740
Almost like the builders were desperately trying to cover something up before anyone saw it.

65
00:04:34,200 --> 00:04:36,180
Like the Academy's doing now.

66
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,520
This place has given me the creeps.

67
00:04:38,560 --> 00:04:39,980
Maybe we should forget the mission, huh?

68
00:04:40,780 --> 00:04:42,220
I hope I see a monster!

69
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:43,680
Don't say stuff like that!

70
00:04:43,720 --> 00:04:44,360
Are you crazy?

71
00:04:50,320 --> 00:04:51,400
No, no, no!

72
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:52,300
Not happening!

73
00:04:52,420 --> 00:04:53,500
I am not going in there!

74
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:55,360
You know I can't deal with creepy stuff!

75
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:58,900
I've even got a doctor's note that specifically says to avoid monsters!

76
00:04:59,220 --> 00:04:59,920
You want to see it?

77
00:05:00,020 --> 00:05:00,760
I'll show it to you.

78
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:02,660
You can calm down.

79
00:05:02,880 --> 00:05:04,800
I'm not taking the two of you with me.

80
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:06,860
Seriously?

81
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:09,680
We don't know what caused the disappearances.

82
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,060
It could be a monster.

83
00:05:11,340 --> 00:05:12,020
Or a virus.

84
00:05:12,420 --> 00:05:14,640
Or maybe even some kind of chemical weapon.

85
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:17,800
But one thing we do know for sure.

86
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:21,180
No human who's ever gone in there has made it back out alive.

87
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:24,740
I can't risk taking you guys in there with me.

88
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:27,620
Not when I have no idea what we'd be up against.

89
00:05:27,620 --> 00:05:30,400
It would simply be too dangerous.

90
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:34,340
Much as I hate to admit it, you've got a point there.

91
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:38,400
I'm guessing that's why Dad sent me instead of one of the other Meisters.

92
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:41,500
My Reaper body is less vulnerable than most.

93
00:05:42,260 --> 00:05:44,220
Even so, this is still dangerous.

94
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:46,260
Yes, but what does that matter?

95
00:05:47,420 --> 00:05:49,860
My Dad has made his policies on this clear.

96
00:05:50,260 --> 00:05:52,320
Our top priority is the magic tools.

97
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:54,240
That's what you're after here?

98
00:05:54,240 --> 00:05:57,760
If I'm not out in 40 minutes, head back for the Academy.

99
00:05:59,140 --> 00:06:00,260
Go straight there.

100
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:02,020
You will not come in after me.

101
00:06:04,440 --> 00:06:08,440
Instead of sending me out to help battle the Keisha, Dad gives me this mission.

102
00:06:09,380 --> 00:06:12,200
Well, soon enough, I'll see what's so important about this tool.

103
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:17,280
We've lost contact with the 13th Squadron.

104
00:06:17,740 --> 00:06:21,240
15 and 17, circle around and attack the enemy in Area 34.

105
00:06:22,880 --> 00:06:25,300
It sounds like it's complete chaos out there.

106
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:28,820
All in all, I'd say it could be going better.

107
00:06:29,280 --> 00:06:31,360
Maybe it's time for us to assume the command.

108
00:06:31,740 --> 00:06:33,200
Then what are we supposed to say?

109
00:06:33,260 --> 00:06:35,180
What orders do we give that will help them?

110
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:39,280
I don't know, but anything would be better than standing here doing nothing while they fight.

111
00:06:39,540 --> 00:06:40,740
Well, that's where you got it wrong.

112
00:06:40,820 --> 00:06:44,260
If we start giving random orders, we could stir up even more confusion.

113
00:06:48,940 --> 00:06:51,020
No, not the scary face again.

114
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,500
Listen to you two.

115
00:06:53,020 --> 00:06:54,680
Sometimes I envy your freedom.

116
00:06:56,100 --> 00:06:59,940
You can go wherever you want, do whatever you want, whenever you want.

117
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,740
You can take real action.

118
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,080
You want chain here.

119
00:07:03,080 --> 00:07:04,580
Know what I mean?

120
00:07:07,340 --> 00:07:08,420
He's got a point.

121
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:09,980
At least we can leave.

122
00:07:10,900 --> 00:07:13,280
I guess we're not the only ones who are frustrated.

123
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:16,660
If his soul wasn't bound to Death's city,

124
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:20,300
Lord Death would have been the first one on that battlefield fighting the Kisha.

125
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,220
Here we are.

126
00:07:28,720 --> 00:07:30,080
The Vanishing Village.

127
00:07:33,080 --> 00:07:54,040
So far I don't sense anything abnormal about this place other than its emptiness.

128
00:07:54,700 --> 00:07:56,040
It's utterly silent.

129
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:59,980
But still, there has to be something here.

130
00:08:08,380 --> 00:08:09,200
What's that?

131
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:27,640
Where the hell am I?

132
00:08:27,640 --> 00:08:32,420
This looks like the inside of some sort of ancient ruin.

133
00:08:34,260 --> 00:08:34,820
Hey!

134
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:36,340
Hey, Boss Man!

135
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:39,140
I'm not your Boss Man.

136
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,000
Please just call me Joe.

137
00:08:42,700 --> 00:08:43,940
Boss, come here!

138
00:08:44,140 --> 00:08:45,340
We've got lunch already.

139
00:08:45,440 --> 00:08:46,520
It's time to eat!

140
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:49,600
I don't care what you say, I'm still not your Boss.

141
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:53,200
Mr. Boss Man, there's coffee down here for you, too.

142
00:08:53,840 --> 00:08:56,720
Boss or not, I can still have a cup of coffee.

143
00:08:59,880 --> 00:09:00,820
The coffee?

144
00:09:02,120 --> 00:09:03,640
Here, have some.

145
00:09:04,160 --> 00:09:06,020
Yummy, yummy coffee!

146
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:10,600
This is the coffee?

147
00:09:17,340 --> 00:09:18,540
This is the tool?

148
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:24,060
Looks like a key.

149
00:09:24,060 --> 00:09:30,500
The biggest key that I've ever seen.

150
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,600
This seems too easy.

151
00:09:33,180 --> 00:09:37,460
I just waltz into a deserted city, grab the magic tool, and walk back out again?

152
00:09:38,540 --> 00:09:39,700
Maybe it's a fake.

153
00:09:40,340 --> 00:09:41,540
If so, it's a good one.

154
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,060
It looks authentic enough to me, anyway.

155
00:09:44,060 --> 00:10:11,160
Hold on.

156
00:10:11,940 --> 00:10:12,760
Slow down!

157
00:10:12,760 --> 00:10:13,900
Maka!

158
00:10:14,980 --> 00:10:16,060
Do you hear me?

159
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:17,620
Stop running!

160
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,700
I know you want to move fast.

161
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,820
But where are you going?

162
00:10:31,180 --> 00:10:32,180
I don't know.

163
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:42,940
Nice one.

164
00:10:43,900 --> 00:10:46,420
Probably should have figured out where we were going first.

165
00:10:46,740 --> 00:10:50,620
I know you want to find Medusa and Crona, but you won't do it running around blindly.

166
00:10:50,940 --> 00:10:53,520
You are familiar with the whole look-before-you-leap thing, right?

167
00:10:54,020 --> 00:10:54,420
Yeah.

168
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:55,920
I know you're right.

169
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:56,560
Sorry.

170
00:10:56,560 --> 00:11:00,360
So, what do you want to do now?

171
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:03,700
Well, I can try using my soul perception.

172
00:11:03,960 --> 00:11:05,320
That should sniff out Medusa.

173
00:11:05,320 --> 00:11:08,960
That won't do any good if she has her soul protect on.

174
00:11:10,100 --> 00:11:10,500
True.

175
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:12,620
But there's still Professor Stein.

176
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:15,560
And Crona and Miss Marie are out there hunting the witch, too.

177
00:11:15,980 --> 00:11:19,160
If I can find any of their souls, they'll lead me to her.

178
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,700
Lovely.

179
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:23,680
So now we've got Professor Stein, who even Lord Death couldn't locate.

180
00:11:23,880 --> 00:11:26,120
And then there's Miss Marie and Crona, who went after him.

181
00:11:26,540 --> 00:11:29,020
We're trying to find three people who could be anywhere in the world,

182
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,660
and we don't have a clue where to start looking.

183
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:31,340
Oh, yeah.

184
00:11:31,380 --> 00:11:32,920
I'm sure that's going to work out perfectly.

185
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:34,960
Don't be so negative, soul.

186
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:36,760
I know it's going to work.

187
00:11:39,280 --> 00:11:40,080
Of course.

188
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,600
I'll still need your help.

189
00:11:43,440 --> 00:11:44,680
Uh, sure thing.

190
00:11:49,160 --> 00:11:52,160
Damn it.

191
00:11:56,160 --> 00:11:59,320
I guess this is the security system guarding the tool.

192
00:12:02,060 --> 00:12:03,480
Are you qualified?

193
00:12:05,320 --> 00:12:08,520
Do you have what it takes to wield the magic tool?

194
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:10,360
Creepy clown.

195
00:12:11,080 --> 00:12:11,880
Who are you?

196
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,600
What are you doing here?

197
00:12:14,180 --> 00:12:16,080
Were you the one who destroyed the village?

198
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:17,320
Answer me.

199
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:28,560
What am I doing here?

200
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:31,460
I prevent meddlesome humans from entering this place.

201
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,420
Or from leaving it alive, at least.

202
00:12:33,520 --> 00:12:36,120
I destroy anyone who touches the magic tool.

203
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:38,940
You're responsible for what happened 20 years ago.

204
00:12:38,940 --> 00:12:41,100
That is correct.

205
00:12:41,400 --> 00:12:44,180
I protect the resting place of the last magic tool.

206
00:12:44,660 --> 00:12:46,420
You killed them all because of the tool?

207
00:12:47,180 --> 00:12:48,760
Those foolish humans.

208
00:12:49,760 --> 00:12:53,720
They dug up this ruin 20 years ago and discovered the tool.

209
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:56,960
They weren't qualified to wield it either.

210
00:12:57,960 --> 00:12:59,360
So I ate them.

211
00:12:59,360 --> 00:13:01,640
I ate them all.

212
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:04,400
They were delicious.

213
00:13:07,440 --> 00:13:09,500
All trespassers must die.

214
00:13:09,940 --> 00:13:11,380
That includes you, too.

215
00:13:13,080 --> 00:13:13,960
Snack time.

216
00:13:16,960 --> 00:13:19,300
You won't make a meal out of me that easily.

217
00:13:20,040 --> 00:13:21,020
Running, are you?

218
00:13:21,020 --> 00:13:23,280
I won't let you get barred.

219
00:13:32,740 --> 00:13:36,540
With a huge body like that, he'll never be able to squeeze in after me.

220
00:13:36,920 --> 00:13:39,000
What a poorly designed security system.

221
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:45,740
Oh, are you stuck?

222
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:53,880
I'm good!

223
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,240
Close one.

224
00:14:04,560 --> 00:14:05,320
But I did it.

225
00:14:05,960 --> 00:14:08,160
Now I just have to make it back to Liz and Patty.

226
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:10,420
What's that?

227
00:14:12,400 --> 00:14:13,360
There are two!

228
00:14:13,740 --> 00:14:14,940
Didn't see that coming!

229
00:14:23,280 --> 00:14:24,320
Chow time!

230
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,340
Oink, oink, oink.

231
00:14:27,960 --> 00:14:29,300
Oink, oink, oink.

232
00:14:30,820 --> 00:14:32,960
Kid sure is taking his time, huh?

233
00:14:33,380 --> 00:14:34,820
There's no reason to worry.

234
00:14:34,940 --> 00:14:37,700
It might take a while, but I'm sure everything will be hunky-dory.

235
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:39,880
If anyone can do it, it's our meister.

236
00:14:40,280 --> 00:14:41,100
Do it, kid!

237
00:14:41,160 --> 00:14:42,160
I believe in you!

238
00:14:42,240 --> 00:14:45,680
But just to be safe, maybe we should go in there and check up on him.

239
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:48,700
What, are you kidding me?

240
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:51,020
We'd be nuts to go into someplace as creepy as that.

241
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:52,460
Do you have a death wish or something?

242
00:14:52,940 --> 00:14:54,100
It'll be fine.

243
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:55,460
I say we go in after him.

244
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:57,260
Seriously?

245
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:00,280
Were you listening to a thing I just said?

246
00:15:01,180 --> 00:15:01,360
Hm?

247
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:03,840
Of course I was.

248
00:15:04,100 --> 00:15:05,760
You said something about a pig, right?

249
00:15:06,620 --> 00:15:09,560
Don't you ever listen when I talk!

250
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:13,360
What's that?

251
00:15:15,240 --> 00:15:15,940
What's what?

252
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:17,400
I don't know what you're talking about!

253
00:15:17,400 --> 00:15:18,360
I didn't hear anything!

254
00:15:18,520 --> 00:15:19,500
Nothing at all!

255
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:31,280
Still coming.

256
00:15:31,280 --> 00:15:32,660
I don't know what you're talking about!

257
00:15:32,660 --> 00:15:33,280
Oh!

258
00:15:35,580 --> 00:15:36,760
Perfect symmetry!

259
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:39,360
No symmetry!

260
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:42,260
Perfect symmetry!

261
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,640
Not symmetrical at all!

262
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:45,960
No, perfectly symmetrical!

263
00:15:46,180 --> 00:15:47,800
No, not symmetrical at all!

264
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,520
What a perfect pose!

265
00:15:51,320 --> 00:15:52,500
Unbelievable beauty!

266
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:54,480
The very definition of symmetry!

267
00:15:57,120 --> 00:15:58,120
Oh, dear!

268
00:15:58,120 --> 00:16:03,200
Oh, the destructive power of true beauty!

269
00:16:14,200 --> 00:16:16,400
A little further, just to that building!

270
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,160
Give it back!

271
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:26,580
Hand over the magic tomb now!

272
00:16:28,120 --> 00:16:45,000
You came after me?

273
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:46,500
Sure!

274
00:16:46,860 --> 00:16:47,980
What else would we do?

275
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:53,200
